## Image Generation (MCP Tool)

The `openclaw-image-gen` MCP server provides AI image generation tools.
It is auto-configured in `.mcp.json` and available to all agents.

### Available tools

- **`generate_image`** — generate an image from a text prompt
  - `prompt` (required) — detailed description of the image
  - `filename` — output name (e.g. `icon-settings-512`)
  - `width` / `height` — pixel dimensions (256-1024, multiples of 64)
  - `style` — art style (e.g. `flat vector`, `pixel art`, `photorealistic`)
  - `output_format` — `png` (default) or `jpg`
  - `backend` — `local` (SDXL Turbo, default), `gemini`, `imagen`, or `openai`
- **`list_image_backends`** — check which backends are configured

### API key resolution

The MCP server resolves API keys in order:
1. Environment variables (`GEMINI_API_KEY`, `OPENAI_API_KEY`)
2. Mission Control vault (fetched from `http://127.0.0.1:8765/api/vault/get/<name>`)

The `local` backend requires no API key — it runs SDXL Turbo on-device.

### Asset organization

All generated images go in the project's `assets/` directory:
```
assets/
  icons/         App icons, toolbar icons
  logos/          Brand logos, wordmarks
  banners/       Hero images, headers
  splash/        Splash screens, loading screens
  backgrounds/   Textures, patterns, gradients
  marketing/     Social media, app store screenshots
  mockups/       UI mockup screenshots
```

Naming convention: `{category}-{name}-{size}.{ext}`
Example: `icon-settings-512.png`, `banner-hero-1024x576.jpg`

### Asset manifest

Maintain `asset-manifest.md` in the project root to track all generated assets.
Update it every time an asset is created, replaced, or deleted.

